+<h2><!--n-->. Six originate document routes answer 500 and log text when a thrown value is unreadable (KS-1868, originate)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> Six outer catch blocks in <code>Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/routes/documents.ts</code> logged <code>error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)</code> with no guard: <code>POST /:id/sign/request</code>, <code>GET /:id/lifecycle-events</code>, <code>GET /:id/sig-json</code>, <code>POST /:id/sign</code>, <code>POST /:id/sign-cert</code> and <code>POST /:id/sign-wallet</code>. A revoked Proxy makes <code>instanceof</code> throw inside the catch; an Error whose <code>message</code> getter throws or returns a value that cannot be turned into text makes the read, or the logger's <code>JSON.stringify</code>, throw. The route then never answered. Each read now sits in an inner try: <code>reason = String(error instanceof Error ? error.message : error)</code>, and a throwing read gives the constant <code>'unreadable thrown value'</code>. Product bytes: <code>documents.ts</code> +42/-6, six hunks.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Two new test files, 26 cells: <code>ks1868-documents-lookup-routes-message-coercion-unreadable-throw.test.ts</code> (the three lookup routes) and <code>ks1868-documents-signing-routes-message-coercion-unreadable-throw.test.ts</code> (the three signing routes), 13 cells each. Controls (C1 to C4) show an ordinary Error and a thrown plain string still answer 500 with their own text; red cells (R1 to R9) show a revoked Proxy, an Error whose message is a null-prototype object and an Error whose message is a Symbol answer 500 and log text. The patches are held Spark passes O83-P2 and O83-P3, applied byte for byte with strict <code>git apply --check -p1</code> (rc 0 on both, and rc 1 on a copy of each with one context line's content corrupted; together, forward and reversed, the same tree). The coordinator ruled the change TIER 1 (Opus gate): the three signing routes write before their catch.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.1 What proves it</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="3"><strong>Red without the change, green with it, and no other cell moves.</strong></td><td> <strong>Red first, by assertion, develop <code>4d1ab2cb6574</code>:</strong> with the two test files and no product change, 9 of 13 failed in each file (R1 to R9), every one with an assertion error and none by crash; the 4 and 4 controls passed.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Whole originate unit suite</strong> (jest): originate 200 files / 2334 tests, then 202 files / <strong>2360 tests, 2360 pass</strong>.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Base against head, twelve thrown values through each lookup route</strong> (the module under test is real, with the held test's module mocks; the logger is the REAL originate winston logger, read from its Console transport; a hang is a null answer at a 1500 ms abort), judged mechanically. An ordinary Error, <code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code> and a plain string are identical at base and head. A <code>BigInt</code> message, a throwing <code>message</code> getter and a revoked Proxy gave NO ANSWER at base (the request was aborted at 1500 ms and no line was logged) and answer 500 <code>INTERNAL_ERROR</code> at head with one logged line; a null, undefined, number, Symbol or cyclic message already answered 500 and now logs a string (<code>"null"</code>, <code>"42"</code>, <code>"Symbol(sym)"</code>, <code>"[object Object]"</code>). 0 rule failures. The three signing routes were NOT recorded this way; they rest on the held cells (below).
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.2 What changes for callers and for the held tests' unhandled-rejection check</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>Hostile thrown values only; a normal error is logged and answered exactly as before.</strong></td><td> The three signing routes share their catch with later steps of each route: <code>sign</code> writes with <code>updateDocument</code> before it, and <code>sign-cert</code> and <code>sign-wallet</code> write with <code>saveDocument</code>. A hostile value thrown after such a write now gets the same constant 500 an ordinary Error gets at that step; the write stays written, as it does for an ordinary Error (read, not run).
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>The held cells' <code>expect(unhandled).toBe(0)</code> is vacuous in this jest environment (measured).</strong> The operator flagged as unmeasured whether <code>process.on('unhandledRejection')</code> fires here. A positive control, a deliberately unhandled rejection made inside the same environment with the same listener, was seen <strong>0 times</strong> (jest-circus reported it as the cell's own failure instead), so that assertion cannot fail. The hang is established by the null answer at the abort, not by the listener.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.3 Environment and figures</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Measured 2026-11-02/03 (UTC) on an Apple Silicon (arm64) Mac, macOS 27.0.1, shared with other seats.</strong></td><td> Node v26.8.1 (not an LTS measurement), TypeScript 5.9.3, jest 29.7.0, eslint 10.7.0; develop <code>4d1ab2cb6574</code> for the base. <code>tsc</code> with the test files in the program (the service tsconfig excludes them; <code>node</code> and <code>jest</code> types), a planted type error reported once as <code>TS2322</code>: <strong>0 errors before and 0 after</strong>. eslint on the two test files: 0 errors, 0 warnings, and a planted file raised <code>no-unused-vars</code> and <code>no-debugger</code>. Originate is not one of the services the test-types ratchet names.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.4 What this does not prove</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>Six catch blocks, not the ticket.</strong></td><td> KS-1868 stays open: it lists 253 catch and log sites that read a thrown value unguarded; this change covers six, in originate's document routes. The other sites are not touched. The goldens are operator-authored: whether a real thrown value of this kind occurs is not shown here.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Not run: a real Postgres, a booted originate service, the three signing routes with the real logger, a hostile value after a write on a real database, the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), Node 24 or any LTS Node, any deploy.
+    </td></tr></table>
